  "id": "t07-014",
  "track": "track-07",
  "title": "HTML forms controls validation and form submission",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "A form control has a type, label, value, form owner, validity state, and serialization behavior.",
    "The browser constructs an ordered entry list from successful controls and submits it using the selected action, method, and encoding.",
    "Input type chooses the control and applicable attributes; autocomplete names the data, while inputmode hints the virtual keyboard.",
    "Constraint validation improves interaction but never replaces server-side validation.",
    "Native HTML forms work without client JavaScript and can be progressively enhanced."
